<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huỳnh Tấn Phát</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Huynh Tan Phat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huỳnh Tấn Phát was a Vietnamese architect and communist politician who helped found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a>. From 1969 he was chairman of the Provisional Revolutionary Government of the Republic of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, the southern insurgency's government during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> peace talks. After reunification in 1976 he became a vice-premier of Vietnam.</p></div>
